---
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';
import game from '../../data/game.json';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
type Check = { values: number; agree: number; max_error_px: number; passed: boolean };
const info = game.info as (Record<string, unknown> & { check?: Check; check3d?: Check; check3d_wrong?: Check; check3r?: Check; check3r_wrong?: Check }) | null;

const tests = [
	{
		id: 'test1',
		name: 'Test 1',
		title: 'The dot on a flat plane',
		text: 'Fortran makes a table of 256 sine values. 8086 Assembly draws the curve and moves a yellow dot along it: left to right, and up and down.',
		check: info?.check,
		expect: 'pass',
	},
	{
		id: 'test2a',
		name: 'Test 2a',
		title: 'The dot in 3D',
		text: 'The same movement, with depth. The curve starts at the back and ends at the front, and its middle point is the center of the 3D space. The A side divides by the distance from the eye.',
		check: info?.check3d,
		expect: 'pass',
	},
	{
		id: 'test2b',
		name: 'Test 2b',
		title: 'Wrong values, and the check',
		text: 'The program of test 2a with one wrong word: SHR, not SAR. Half of the dots go to wrong places. The check finds each wrong point, so a wrong program cannot get onto the site.',
		check: info?.check3d_wrong,
		expect: 'fail',
	},
	{
		id: 'test3a',
		name: 'Test 3a',
		title: 'The wave turns',
		text: 'The wave of test 2 goes from the back to the front. Now it turns around the center of the 3D space, and the dot moves along it. The A side turns each point with the sine and the cosine of the turn.',
		check: info?.check3r,
		expect: 'pass',
	},
	{
		id: 'test3b',
		name: 'Test 3b',
		title: 'A wrong quarter turn',
		text: 'The program of test 3a with one wrong value: 90 (a quarter turn in degrees), not 64 (a quarter turn in 256 steps). The ring becomes a tilted oval, and the wave grows and shrinks as it turns.',
		check: info?.check3r_wrong,
		expect: 'fail',
	},
];
---

<StarlightPage
	frontmatter={{
		title: 'The game: all tests',
		description: 'The tests of the game, one step at a time. Each test is a small 8086 program that runs in the browser, and a Fortran check that proves that its answers are correct.',
		tableOfContents: false,
		editUrl: false,
	}}
>
	<div class="wide-page game-page">
		<p class="lead">
			The game grows one test at a time. In each test, Fortran (the B side) does the maths, and 8086 Assembly (the A
			side) draws in a copy of a 1980s PC. A check then compares the answers of the two sides. GitHub Actions runs all
			checks for each change. If a check fails, the site does not change.
		</p>

		<ol class="test-list">
			{tests.map((t) => (
				<li class={`test-card ${t.expect === 'fail' ? 'is-wrong' : ''}`}>
					<a href={`${base}/game/${t.id}/`}>
						<span class="test-name">{t.name}</span>
						<span class="test-title">{t.title}</span>
					</a>
					<p class="small">{t.text}</p>
					{t.check ? (
						<p class="small test-result">
							{t.expect === 'pass' ? (
								<><span class="ok">✓ The check passes:</span> {t.check.agree} of {t.check.values} answers agree.</>
							) : (
								<><span class="bad">✗ The check fails, as it must:</span> only {t.check.agree} of {t.check.values} answers agree.</>
							)}
						</p>
					) : (
						<p class="small muted">The game build is missing on this computer. Run <code>game/dev.sh</code>.</p>
					)}
				</li>
			))}
		</ol>

		<h2>Next</h2>
		<p>
			The game is a small lander game (decision D20). The tests come first, so that each new part of the maths has a
			check before the game uses it. The files are in the folder <a href="https://github.com/kairin/000-111-learn/tree/main/game"><code>game/</code></a>.
		</p>
	</div>
</StarlightPage>
